# Anti-Drift Policy

Anchor enforces this policy on all work in opted-in repositories.

- PRs must align with the active phase or named plan entry in `~/.anchor/<repo-slug>/plan.md` (or an explicit `/anchor-plan` record).
- PR description length should be proportional to diff size. Long prose with minimal diff is a smell.
- Any change touching only infra/ops paths on a non-infra branch requires either an `infra:` prefix or a plan note justifying the deviation.
- Behavior-affecting changes must include or update tests.
- Titles or bodies containing "stub", "placeholder", "TODO follow-up", "out of scope", "for now", or similar language trigger enforcement.
- Anchor will comment and may block PRs that pad scope, hand-wave verification, or shift goalposts instead of completing the stated task.